\name{cellucid_history_replay}
\alias{cellucid_history_replay}
\title{Replay a saved history}
\usage{
cellucid_history_replay(viewer, saved, branch, mapping, name, tracker)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{saved}{A saved state of this browser (history_saved_list). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{branch}{Its branch; its main branch when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{mapping}{Names to use in place of the recorded ones, each from its recorded name (the replay report offers them: a step's missing names what matched nothing here). A category is named by its field's recorded key. A named list. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does). \describe{\item{\code{categories}}{Categories: in a field (its recorded key), recorded label \ifelse{latex}{<U+2192>}{→} label here. A vector or list of a named list. Required.}\item{\code{fields}}{obs fields: recorded key \ifelse{latex}{<U+2192>}{→} key here. A vector or list of a named list. Required.}\item{\code{genes}}{Genes: recorded name \ifelse{latex}{<U+2192>}{→} name here. A vector or list of a named list. Required.}}}
\item{name}{A name, unique among its kind (compared without case and extra spaces); no length limit. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{tracker}{Its tracker, by name or id; its tracker shown when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{report} (Every step replayed and what became of it), \code{tracker}.
}
\description{
Apply a saved state's branch (its main branch when left out) again here, step by step by name, in a new tracker linked to it; with a mapping, other names are used for fields, categories and genes. The report says what did not match.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.replay} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_replay(viewer, saved = "state-1")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
